Approach: Sorting + Two Pointer
First, sort the array.
Fix one element i (from 0 to n-1).
Use two pointers:
j = i + 1
k = n - 1
Calculate sum:
If sum == 0 → store triplet, move both pointers
If sum > 0 → decrease k
If sum < 0 → increase j
Skip duplicates:
If nums[i] == nums[i-1] → continue
After finding triplet → skip duplicate j and k

Time Complexity: O(n^2)
Space Complexity: O(1) (excluding output)
